# Line endings are not cosmetic here. `check_surface.sh` compares the symbols in the built
# library against `foundationdb.allow` line by line, so a CRLF checkout makes every listed
# symbol miss its match — and the check then reports the same 19 symbols as both unlisted
# and unused, which reads as a total surface violation rather than as a checkout artefact.
# It cost a debugging round on Windows to find that, so the rule is written down instead.
#
# Every shell script here is also run under `sh`, which reads `#!/bin/sh\r` as an
# interpreter named `/bin/sh\r` and reports "bad interpreter".
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.allow         text eol=lf
ci.sh           text eol=lf
*.c             text eol=lf
*.h             text eol=lf
*.cpp           text eol=lf
*.lean          text eol=lf
